  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Let \\(f\\) be a function satisfying \\(f(xy) = \\dfrac{f(x)}{y}\\) for all positive real numbers \\(x\\) and \\(y.\\) If \\(f(500) = 3,\\) what is the value of \\(f(600)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\)",
    "B": "\\(2\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(3\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{18}{5}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "To use the known value \\(f(500)\\), choose \\(x=500\\). We then want \\(xy=600\\), so take \\(y=600/500=6/5\\). Both inputs are positive, as required by the identity. Therefore\n\\[\nf(600)=\\frac{f(500)}{6/5}\n=3\\cdot\\frac56\n=\\boxed{\\frac52}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{C}\\).",
